! NAME: BTM & RMAN Handover
! DESC: Zero-Latency Protocols for Rogue Linux
! PHASE: 4 FINAL

# SUMMARY
The Cogman extra modules provide the backbone for ultra-fast system awareness.

## COMPONENTS
* btm.h : Binary struct definitions for mmap access.
* rman.h : Tactical ASCII identifiers for HUD rendering.
* btm_forge : Pre-compiler for metadata blobs.
* btm_read : Reference reader using mmap().

## ZERO-LATENCY ACCESS
> ./btm_read test.btm

* Metadata access: < 0.001ms (Zero CPU parsing).
* Documentation: Embedded directly in BTM, no extra disk seeks.

? WARNING: All package metadata must be pre-compiled to .btm using btm_forge before rootfs deployment.
? ALERT: RMAN v2 requires an ANSI-compliant terminal for HUD coloring.

**The Cogman extra modules are forged and ready for the rootfs phase.**
